#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166592 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166754 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8e25ae0e-d10c-5fa4-924e-4c6a7efebac6" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Sinh Function"}] :question/id #uuid "181b2a5e-7caf-5527-8602-e67a945affde" :question/math-academy-id "e-8337" :question/problem "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nIf $y = 2\\arsinh{x^2},$ then find $\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}.$" :question/worked-solution "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic sine function is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}(\\arsinh x) = \\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{x^2+1}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{({x}^{2})}^{2}+1}}\\cdot {({x}^{2})}^{′} \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{4}+1}}\\cdot 2x \\\\  & =\\frac{4x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{4}+1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166593 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166755 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "eaab6e41-d34d-5eca-a41f-5ebe58a6b178" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Cosh Function"}] :question/id #uuid "ce19d882-3c04-5ef1-8393-7de582df188d" :question/math-academy-id "e-8338" :question/problem "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nIf $y =\\arcosh(x+1),$ then find $\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}.$" :question/worked-solution "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cosine function is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}(\\arcosh x) = \\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{x^2-1}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡(x+1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(x+1)^{2}-1}}\\cdot (x+1)^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{({x}^{2}+2x+1)-1}}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+2x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x(x+2)}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166594 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166756 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1979b91d-2ac0-5d35-b4cc-1c9c9505b503" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Tanh Function"}] :question/id #uuid "d5eeb5a1-4bfd-5f1e-b261-548c91eec64b" :question/math-academy-id "e-8339" :question/problem "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nIf $y = \\artanh{4x},$ then find $\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}.$" :question/worked-solution "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic tangent function is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}(\\artanh x) = \\dfrac{1}{1-x^2}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{artanh}⁡4x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1-{(4x)}^{2}}\\cdot {(4x)}^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1-16{x}^{2}}\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{1-16{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166595 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166757 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "57d851ce-44b5-5713-ba65-7f5a9cc1122f" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Inverse Hyperbolic Functions Using the Product and Quotient Rules"}] :question/id #uuid "7cd3958b-aa1c-5c9a-b2ef-a21002aa7ff1" :question/math-academy-id "e-8340" :question/problem "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nIf $w(x) = e^{2x}\\artanh{x},$ then $w'(x)=2e^{2x}\\artanh{x} + y(x).$ What is $y(x)?$" :question/worked-solution "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nHere, we have the product of two functions $u(x) = e^{2x}$ and $v(x)=\\artanh{x}.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{w}^{′}(x) & ={({e}^{2x})}^{′}\\cdot \\operatorname{artanh}⁡x+{e}^{2x}\\cdot {(\\operatorname{artanh}⁡x)}^{′} \\\\  & =2{e}^{2x}\\cdot \\operatorname{artanh}⁡x+{e}^{2x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =2{e}^{2x}\\operatorname{artanh}⁡x+{{\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{1-{x}^{2}}}_{⏟}}_{y(x)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y(x) = \\dfrac{e^{2x}}{1 - x^2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186516767 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166756 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1979b91d-2ac0-5d35-b4cc-1c9c9505b503" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Tanh Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "678a9ad5-1c9d-5e0a-b721-d649b8029905" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x(1-x)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516336}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "678a9ad5-1c9d-5e0a-b721-d649b8029905" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x(1-x)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516336} :answer-field/id #uuid "2c15bd43-7acb-5fe5-ae71-e05e3f9b122f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516666}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "032db788-5417-5a60-9bc5-91af6b1ca366" :question/math-academy-id "q-337914" :question/problem "$$\n\nIf $y=2\\,\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(2x-1),$ calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "$$\n\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic tangent function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{artanh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(2x-1)) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(2x-1)) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{1-{(2x-1)}^{2}}\\cdot {(2x-1)}^{′} \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{1-(4{x}^{2}-4x+1)}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{1}{4x-4{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{4x(1-x)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x(1-x)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186516766 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166754 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8e25ae0e-d10c-5fa4-924e-4c6a7efebac6" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Sinh Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a6c5edf-783c-518f-ae3c-3b3aa9ea7ef9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{\\sqrt{9x^2+1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516400}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8a6c5edf-783c-518f-ae3c-3b3aa9ea7ef9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{\\sqrt{9x^2+1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516400} :answer-field/id #uuid "4549f7e1-46e1-5da6-bdca-f119837ee94a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516675}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "02e5e578-2923-57b2-a053-9b7f26dd5f2f" :question/math-academy-id "q-341798" :question/problem "$$\n\nIf $y=5\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡(3x),$ calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "$$\n\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic sine function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡(3x)) \\\\  & =5\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡(3x)) \\\\  & =5\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(3x)^{2}+1}}\\cdot (3x)^{′} \\\\  & =5\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{9{x}^{2}+1}}\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{\\sqrt{9{x}^{2}+1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186516831 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166754 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8e25ae0e-d10c-5fa4-924e-4c6a7efebac6" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Sinh Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ce1e87fa-a67e-5e2b-a4d6-91106614efde" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-6x+18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516548}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ce1e87fa-a67e-5e2b-a4d6-91106614efde" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-6x+18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516548} :answer-field/id #uuid "5a6982d7-16d9-5cb0-8eec-9bbb54099cee" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516686}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a4eeca3f-6b34-52eb-84b0-9a3e73ae1349" :question/math-academy-id "q-341812" :question/problem "$$\n\nIf $y=arsinh\\,(\\frac{x-3}{3}),$ calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n| $\\text{d}y$ | $=$ | $1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{d}x$ |  | {{field-1}} |" :question/worked-solution "$$\n\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic sine function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\,(arsinh\\,(\\frac{x-3}{3})) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{(\\frac{x-3}{3})}^{2}+1}}\\cdot {(\\frac{x-3}{3})}^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{9}+1}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{\\frac{(x-3)^{2}+9}{9}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(x-3)^{2}+9}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{({x}^{2}-6x+9)+9}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-6x+18}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186516832 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166754 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8e25ae0e-d10c-5fa4-924e-4c6a7efebac6" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Sinh Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a559b83c-53ab-5a83-9edd-ae76985624bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{4x^8+9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516457}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a559b83c-53ab-5a83-9edd-ae76985624bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{4x^8+9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516457} :answer-field/id #uuid "6349b651-0355-5796-8a79-80d15ad9f15e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516693}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "aa4e4da2-fcbb-5aa7-a6f1-72dee8a3b1b4" :question/math-academy-id "q-341820" :question/problem "$$\n\nIf $y=3\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡(\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{4}),$ calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n| $\\text{d}y$ | $=$ | $24{x}^{3}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{d}x$ |  | {{field-1}} |" :question/worked-solution "$$\n\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic sine function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡(\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{4})) \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡(\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{4})) \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{(\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{4})}^{2}+1}}\\cdot {(\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{4})}^{′} \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{\\frac{4}{9}{x}^{8}+1}}\\cdot \\frac{8}{3}{x}^{3} \\\\  & =8\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{3}}{\\sqrt{\\frac{4{x}^{8}+9}{9}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{24{x}^{3}}{\\sqrt{4{x}^{8}+9}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186516800 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166756 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1979b91d-2ac0-5d35-b4cc-1c9c9505b503" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Tanh Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d7221748-06ef-513f-b4e9-e3cda3bc4151" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{x(1-2x)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516566}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d7221748-06ef-513f-b4e9-e3cda3bc4151" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{x(1-2x)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516566} :answer-field/id #uuid "0118df54-580d-5a48-9cc7-35323ba1fc0f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516649}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4b8c9d43-7595-500c-b3ee-cac3fe18402d" :question/math-academy-id "q-344313" :question/problem "$$\n\nIf $y=4\\,\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(4x-1),$ calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "$$\n\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic tangent function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{artanh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(4x-1)) \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(4x-1)) \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{1}{1-(4x-1)^{2}}\\cdot (4x-1)^{′} \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{1}{1-(16{x}^{2}-8x+1)}\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =16\\cdot \\frac{1}{8x-16{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =16\\cdot \\frac{1}{8x(1-2x)} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{x(1-2x)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186516789 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166754 :knowl