mula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic sine function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡2{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡2{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{(2{x}^{2})}^{2}+1}}\\cdot {(2{x}^{2})}^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4{x}^{4}+1}}\\cdot 4x \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{4{x}^{4}+1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186516779 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166755 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "eaab6e41-d34d-5eca-a41f-5ebe58a6b178" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Cosh Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5e0efab3-b17a-5e69-ad24-7e9b0adde363" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{6}-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516314} {:answer/id #uuid "6edace4c-58d5-5508-b8f8-8619c6a00614" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{6}-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516358} {:answer/id #uuid "b94fbfce-4686-563a-9aff-8af49a27dc6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{3}-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516498} {:answer/id #uuid "c52a5170-150c-5577-834a-77187a9e9f58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9{x}^{2}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{6}-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516530} {:answer/id #uuid "c86c1d3c-651a-597b-9885-c1f6e5ddb575" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9{x}^{2}}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{6}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516536}] :